  "ch2.limit": "Single-byte XOR provides obfuscation rather than cryptographic strength. All real security in this hybrid container rests on the 1040-byte AES block segment at the front.",
  "ch3.title": "Why You Can Spot ECB vs CBC at a Glance",
  "toc.ch3": "Spotting ECB vs CBC",
  "ch3.law": "ECB encrypts each 16-byte block independently: whenever two completely different images share an identical plaintext block, their ciphertext blocks match byte for byte.",
  "ch3.p1": "AES itself maps 16 bytes to 16 bytes; encrypting longer data requires a <strong>block cipher mode</strong>. The two classic choices are <strong>ECB (Electronic Codebook)</strong> and <strong>CBC (Cipher Block Chaining)</strong>:",
  "ch3.m1": "Under <strong>ECB</strong>, each block enters `AES(K)` independently. When two different images both have `aes_size = 1024`, their 65th block is always sixteen `0x10` bytes, so their 65th ciphertext block is <strong>byte-for-byte identical</strong>.",
  "ch3.m2": "Under <strong>CBC</strong>, each plaintext block is XORed with the <strong>previous ciphertext block</strong> before encryption. A single differing byte earlier in the image avalanches forward, making the 65th ciphertext blocks completely unrelated.",
  "ch3.p2": "Comparing offsets `1039..1055` across three unrelated JPEG thumbnails and a full PNG showed the exact same 16-byte ciphertext in all four files. Without reading a single line of code, that proves the client uses <strong>AES-ECB</strong> with one shared key across images.",
  "dg.ecb.cap": "Fig 3. Encrypting the same 16 × 0x10 padding block: ECB produces identical ciphertext across all images, whereas CBC mixes in the prior ciphertext block so every image differs.",
  "dg.ecb.aria": "Diagram: comparing AES-ECB and AES-CBC on the trailing PKCS#7 padding block",
  "dg.ecb.t1": "ECB Mode: Independent Blocks",
  "dg.ecb.same": "Identical Block 65 ciphertext",
  "dg.ecb.t2": "CBC Mode: Chained Feedback",
  "dg.ecb.diff": "Different Block 65 ciphertext",
  "ch3.model.title": "Compare ECB and CBC Ciphertext Propagation",
  "ch3.model.how": "Toggle between ECB and CBC and change whether the two images share their first block, watching whether the trailing padding block (block 4) collides.",
  "ch3.ctl.mode": "Block mode",
